\doxysubsection{Function Documentation}
\Hypertarget{SDL_8h_a8fc8d35348d7c74bad8392d776c937b8}\index{SDL.h@{SDL.h}!SDL\_Init@{SDL\_Init}}
\index{SDL\_Init@{SDL\_Init}!SDL.h@{SDL.h}}
\doxysubsubsection{\texorpdfstring{SDL\_Init()}{SDL\_Init()}}
{\footnotesize\ttfamily \label{SDL_8h_a8fc8d35348d7c74bad8392d776c937b8} 
DECLSPEC int SDLCALL SDL\+\_\+\+Init (\begin{DoxyParamCaption}\item[{Uint32}]{flags}{}\end{DoxyParamCaption})\hspace{0.3cm}{\ttfamily [extern]}}

Initialize the SDL library.

\doxylink{SDL_8h_a8fc8d35348d7c74bad8392d776c937b8}{SDL\+\_\+\+Init()} simply forwards to calling \doxylink{SDL_8h_adfbfddc0ec609b5e5e5cb1c89298e4db}{SDL\+\_\+\+Init\+Sub\+System()}. Therefore, the two may be used interchangeably. Though for readability of your code \doxylink{SDL_8h_adfbfddc0ec609b5e5e5cb1c89298e4db}{SDL\+\_\+\+Init\+Sub\+System()} might be preferred.

The file I/O (for example\+: SDL\+\_\+\+RWFrom\+File) and threading (SDL\+\_\+\+Create\+Thread) subsystems are initialized by default. Message boxes (SDL\+\_\+\+Show\+Simple\+Message\+Box) also attempt to work without initializing the video subsystem, in hopes of being useful in showing an error dialog when SDL\+\_\+\+Init fails. You must specifically initialize other subsystems if you use them in your application.

Logging (such as SDL\+\_\+\+Log) works without initialization, too.

{\ttfamily flags} may be any of the following OR\textquotesingle{}d together\+:


\begin{DoxyItemize}
\item {\ttfamily SDL\+\_\+\+INIT\+\_\+\+TIMER}\+: timer subsystem
\item {\ttfamily SDL\+\_\+\+INIT\+\_\+\+AUDIO}\+: audio subsystem
\item {\ttfamily \doxylink{SDL_8h_afc988e510ed522628ffeb7c76f80c233}{SDL\+\_\+\+INIT\+\_\+\+VIDEO}}\+: video subsystem; automatically initializes the events subsystem
\item {\ttfamily \doxylink{SDL_8h_ad6b47d785eaa00d9c48e6c1cff4aef4b}{SDL\+\_\+\+INIT\+\_\+\+JOYSTICK}}\+: joystick subsystem; automatically initializes the events subsystem
\item {\ttfamily SDL\+\_\+\+INIT\+\_\+\+HAPTIC}\+: haptic (force feedback) subsystem
\item {\ttfamily \doxylink{SDL_8h_ac224a9aa4208de0e9b03948ff9b5fe0a}{SDL\+\_\+\+INIT\+\_\+\+GAMECONTROLLER}}\+: controller subsystem; automatically initializes the joystick subsystem
\item {\ttfamily SDL\+\_\+\+INIT\+\_\+\+EVENTS}\+: events subsystem
\item {\ttfamily SDL\+\_\+\+INIT\+\_\+\+EVERYTHING}\+: all of the above subsystems
\item {\ttfamily \doxylink{SDL_8h_ab848174dfbc69cb2cc7bbf06a6e5c584}{SDL\+\_\+\+INIT\+\_\+\+NOPARACHUTE}}\+: compatibility; this flag is ignored
\end{DoxyItemize}

Subsystem initialization is ref-\/counted, you must call \doxylink{SDL_8h_a14e9091982e09097985e10e3ca65debb}{SDL\+\_\+\+Quit\+Sub\+System()} for each \doxylink{SDL_8h_adfbfddc0ec609b5e5e5cb1c89298e4db}{SDL\+\_\+\+Init\+Sub\+System()} to correctly shutdown a subsystem manually (or call \doxylink{SDL_8h_afdabaf714781099083592051f2d9ac11}{SDL\+\_\+\+Quit()} to force shutdown). If a subsystem is already loaded then this call will increase the ref-\/count and return.


\begin{DoxyParams}{Parameters}
{\em flags} & subsystem initialization flags. \\
\hline
\end{DoxyParams}
\begin{DoxyReturn}{Returns}
0 on success or a negative error code on failure; call SDL\+\_\+\+Get\+Error() for more information.
\end{DoxyReturn}
\begin{DoxySince}{Since}
This function is available since SDL 2.\+0.\+0.
\end{DoxySince}
