\Hypertarget{SDL_8h_afdabaf714781099083592051f2d9ac11}\index{SDL.h@{SDL.h}!SDL\_Quit@{SDL\_Quit}}
\index{SDL\_Quit@{SDL\_Quit}!SDL.h@{SDL.h}}
\doxysubsubsection{\texorpdfstring{SDL\_Quit()}{SDL\_Quit()}}
{\footnotesize\ttfamily \label{SDL_8h_afdabaf714781099083592051f2d9ac11} 
DECLSPEC void SDLCALL SDL\+\_\+\+Quit (\begin{DoxyParamCaption}\item[{void}]{}{}\end{DoxyParamCaption})\hspace{0.3cm}{\ttfamily [extern]}}

Clean up all initialized subsystems.

You should call this function even if you have already shutdown each initialized subsystem with \doxylink{SDL_8h_a14e9091982e09097985e10e3ca65debb}{SDL\+\_\+\+Quit\+Sub\+System()}. It is safe to call this function even in the case of errors in initialization.

If you start a subsystem using a call to that subsystem\textquotesingle{}s init function (for example SDL\+\_\+\+Video\+Init()) instead of \doxylink{SDL_8h_a8fc8d35348d7c74bad8392d776c937b8}{SDL\+\_\+\+Init()} or \doxylink{SDL_8h_adfbfddc0ec609b5e5e5cb1c89298e4db}{SDL\+\_\+\+Init\+Sub\+System()}, then you must use that subsystem\textquotesingle{}s quit function (SDL\+\_\+\+Video\+Quit()) to shut it down before calling \doxylink{SDL_8h_afdabaf714781099083592051f2d9ac11}{SDL\+\_\+\+Quit()}. But generally, you should not be using those functions directly anyhow; use \doxylink{SDL_8h_a8fc8d35348d7c74bad8392d776c937b8}{SDL\+\_\+\+Init()} instead.

You can use this function with atexit() to ensure that it is run when your application is shutdown, but it is not wise to do this from a library or other dynamically loaded code.

\begin{DoxySince}{Since}
This function is available since SDL 2.\+0.\+0.
\end{DoxySince}
\begin{DoxySeeAlso}{See also}
\doxylink{SDL_8h_a8fc8d35348d7c74bad8392d776c937b8}{SDL\+\_\+\+Init} 

\doxylink{SDL_8h_a14e9091982e09097985e10e3ca65debb}{SDL\+\_\+\+Quit\+Sub\+System} 
\end{DoxySeeAlso}
\Hypertarget{SDL_8h_a14e9091982e09097985e10e3ca65debb}\index{SDL.h@{SDL.h}!SDL\_QuitSubSystem@{SDL\_QuitSubSystem}}
\index{SDL\_QuitSubSystem@{SDL\_QuitSubSystem}!SDL.h@{SDL.h}}
\doxysubsubsection{\texorpdfstring{SDL\_QuitSubSystem()}{SDL\_QuitSubSystem()}}
{\footnotesize\ttfamily \label{SDL_8h_a14e9091982e09097985e10e3ca65debb} 
DECLSPEC void SDLCALL SDL\+\_\+\+Quit\+Sub\+System (\begin{DoxyParamCaption}\item[{Uint32}]{flags}{}\end{DoxyParamCaption})\hspace{0.3cm}{\ttfamily [extern]}}

Shut down specific SDL subsystems.

If you start a subsystem using a call to that subsystem\textquotesingle{}s init function (for example SDL\+\_\+\+Video\+Init()) instead of \doxylink{SDL_8h_a8fc8d35348d7c74bad8392d776c937b8}{SDL\+\_\+\+Init()} or \doxylink{SDL_8h_adfbfddc0ec609b5e5e5cb1c89298e4db}{SDL\+\_\+\+Init\+Sub\+System()}, \doxylink{SDL_8h_a14e9091982e09097985e10e3ca65debb}{SDL\+\_\+\+Quit\+Sub\+System()} and \doxylink{SDL_8h_a04dc570990c697eed95681216801710d}{SDL\+\_\+\+Was\+Init()} will not work. You will need to use that subsystem\textquotesingle{}s quit function (SDL\+\_\+\+Video\+Quit()) directly instead. But generally, you should not be using those functions directly anyhow; use \doxylink{SDL_8h_a8fc8d35348d7c74bad8392d776c937b8}{SDL\+\_\+\+Init()} instead.

You still need to call \doxylink{SDL_8h_afdabaf714781099083592051f2d9ac11}{SDL\+\_\+\+Quit()} even if you close all open subsystems with \doxylink{SDL_8h_a14e9091982e09097985e10e3ca65debb}{SDL\+\_\+\+Quit\+Sub\+System()}.


\begin{DoxyParams}{Parameters}
{\em flags} & any of the flags used by \doxylink{SDL_8h_a8fc8d35348d7c74bad8392d776c937b8}{SDL\+\_\+\+Init()}; see SDL\+\_\+\+Init for details.\\
\hline
\end{DoxyParams}
\begin{DoxySince}{Since}
This function is available since SDL 2.\+0.\+0.
\end{DoxySince}
\begin{DoxySeeAlso}{See also}
\doxylink{SDL_8h_adfbfddc0ec609b5e5e5cb1c89298e4db}{SDL\+\_\+\+Init\+Sub\+System} 

\doxylink{SDL_8h_afdabaf714781099083592051f2d9ac11}{SDL\+\_\+\+Quit} 
\end{DoxySeeAlso}
